@startuml
' Which value wins when more than one source could supply the same field.
'
' The rule is "most specific first", applied by layering the page's values on
' top of a base built from the panel and the environment. Nothing is ever
' overwritten with a less specific value.

title Metadata resolution order

skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #ffffff
  BorderColor #475569
  DiamondBackgroundColor #f8fafc
}

start

:resolveSeoData();

if (Did the page publish a SeoData?) then (yes)
    :Use the page's SeoData.;
else (no)
    if (Is panel-level seoData() configured?) then (yes)
        :Use the panel's SeoData.;
    else (no)
        :Start from an empty SeoData.;
    endif
endif

if (Is site_name configured?) then (yes)
    :Layer in the configured site name.;
else (no)
    :Layer in the application name.;
endif

if (Is canonical_fallback enabled?) then (yes)
    :Layer in the current request URL.;
else (no)
    :Leave the canonical URL empty.;
endif

stop

note right
  __Layered underneath__ means each of
  these is only used when nothing
  more specific supplied a value,
  so a page that names its own site
  or canonical keeps it.
end note

@enduml
